cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SURPASS in published work, please cite this software release."
title: "SURPASS: Surface and Passivation Analysis for Semiconductor Systems"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-02
authors:
  - family-names: Macco
    given-names: Bart
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1197-441X"
    affiliation: "Plasma & Materials Processing Group, Eindhoven University of Technology"
    email: "b.macco@tue.nl"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/TUe-PMP/surpass"
url: "https://github.com/TUe-PMP/surpass"
abstract: >-
  SURPASS is a Python package for coupled semiconductor bulk, optical,
  transport, surface-electrostatic, interface-recombination, and
  photoluminescence calculations. Version 1.0.0 is the archived implementation
  used for the POx/AlOx-on-InP passivation study.
keywords:
  - semiconductor physics
  - surface passivation
  - interface states
  - carrier transport
  - photoluminescence
